### Describe the bug

When `RequestDelegateGenerator` decides whether it should intercept an endpoint call it uses the name of the method (_KnownMethods_) and part of the signature (Last argument should be a `System.Delegate`). This makes it intercept method calls that uses the same signature but that are not ment to be intercepted.

Easiest fix would be to just check the containing assembly inside the [`InvocationOperationExtensions.IsValidOperation`](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/blob/main/src/Http/Http.Extensions/gen/StaticRouteHandlerModel/InvocationOperationExtensions.cs#L26) method or something similar

E.g.

```C#
private const string KnownAssembly = "Microsoft.AspNetCore.Routing";

public static readonly string[] KnownMethods =
{
...
};

public static bool IsValidOperation(this IOperation? operation, WellKnownTypes wellKnownTypes, [NotNullWhen(true)] out IInvocationOperation? invocationOperation)
{
    invocationOperation = null;
    if (operation is IInvocationOperation targetOperation &&
        targetOperation.Type?.ContainingAssembly.Identity.Name == KnownAssembly &&
....
```

### Expected Behavior

Only _Map_ methods defined inside the `Microsoft.AspNetCore.Builder` namespace should be intercepted. Don't only rely on the name / signature but also include the assembly/namespace or something else that distinctly tells you it's one of the methods within the aspnet core framework.

### Steps To Reproduce

Run the following sample program with Aot enabled

```C#
var builder = WebApplication.CreateSlimBuilder(args);
builder.Services.Map(() => Task.CompletedTask);
var app = builder.Build();
app.Map("route", () => Results.Text("Working"));
app.Run();

static class Ext
{
    public static IServiceCollection Map(this IServiceCollection services, Delegate @delegate) => services;
}
```

### Exceptions (if any)

```Cannot intercept method 'Ext.Map(IServiceCollection, Delegate)' with interceptor 'GeneratedRouteBuilderExtensionsCore.Map0(IEndpointRouteBuilder, string, Delegate)' because the signatures do not match.```

### .NET Version

8.0.100-rc.1.23455.8

